.TH XFMD 1 "2026-09-12" "xfmd 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
xfmd \- native FOX Markdown viewer and editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xfmd
.RI [ directory | file.md | file.txt ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read and edit local UTF-8 Markdown and text files using FOX.
Markdown is rendered natively without a browser engine or network resource loading.
.SH WORK PATHS
Without an argument the expanded tree starts at the home directory.
A directory argument sets the tree root; "xfmd ." uses the current working directory.
A file argument opens the document with its parent directory as the work path.
Double-click the root to widen to home, then to /. Right-click a directory and
choose Set work path. Click a historic work path below the tree to reactivate it.
The 32 most recent distinct work paths persist between runs.
.PP
The *.md and *.txt toggles are ORed, then intersected with the filename filter.
Both toggles are initially off (all file types). Plain text matches a substring;
? matches one Unicode character and * zero or more characters in the full filename.
Matching ignores ASCII case. Filtering searches descendants in the background,
showing matching files and their ancestor directories. Refresh rescans the tree.
Directory symlinks are not traversed. File symlinks outside the root are omitted.
.SH KEYS
Ctrl+O opens a file. Ctrl+S saves. Ctrl+Shift+S saves under another name.
Ctrl+Z and Ctrl+Y undo and redo. Ctrl+F searches.
Ctrl+1 shows preview, Ctrl+2 the editor, Ctrl+3 split view.
F10 toggles the sidebar. Alt+Left and Alt+Right traverse document history.
Ctrl+Q quits after checking unsaved changes.
.SH LIMITS
Files must be UTF-8 and no larger than 8 MiB. NUL bytes are rejected.
Local links are supported; fragments, remote resources and scripts are not executed.
Images are represented by alt-text placeholders. The parser uses CommonMark 0.31.1
without extension dialects. Glyph coverage depends on installed fonts.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xfe (1),
.BR xfw (1),
.BR xfi (1)
